WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.712
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.012 --> 00:00:08.444
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.744 --> 00:00:15.124
Unit twenty-three: Planning a Party. In this unit, you will make plans and decisions for an event.

4
00:00:16.117 --> 00:00:16.828
Party.

5
00:00:17.528 --> 00:00:20.328
Party means an event where people celebrate together.

6
00:00:20.628 --> 00:00:22.372
We're having a party on Friday.

7
00:00:23.072 --> 00:00:25.481
Your turn. Say: Party.

8
00:00:28.181 --> 00:00:28.880
Party.

9
00:00:29.883 --> 00:00:30.815
Invite.

10
00:00:31.515 --> 00:00:34.292
Invite means to ask someone to come to an event.

11
00:00:34.592 --> 00:00:36.069
We will invite our parents.

12
00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:39.770
Your turn. Say: Invite.

13
00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:43.401
Invite.

14
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:45.174
Guest.

15
00:00:45.874 --> 00:00:48.024
Guest means a person who is invited.

16
00:00:48.324 --> 00:00:49.894
There will be thirty guests.

17
00:00:50.594 --> 00:00:52.910
Your turn. Say: Guest.

18
00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:56.425
Guest.

19
00:00:57.417 --> 00:00:58.348
Decorate.

20
00:00:59.048 --> 00:01:02.394
Decorate means to make a place look nice for a special day.

21
00:01:02.694 --> 00:01:04.392
Let's decorate the classroom.

22
00:01:05.092 --> 00:01:07.350
Your turn. Say: Decorate.

23
00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.028
Decorate.

24
00:01:12.017 --> 00:01:12.693
Food.

25
00:01:13.393 --> 00:01:15.288
Food means things that people eat.

26
00:01:15.588 --> 00:01:17.460
Everyone will bring some food.

27
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.580
Your turn. Say: Food.

28
00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:24.025
Food.

29
00:01:25.017 --> 00:01:25.913
Music.

30
00:01:26.613 --> 00:01:29.251
Music means songs and sounds to enjoy.

31
00:01:29.551 --> 00:01:30.843
Who will play the music?

32
00:01:31.543 --> 00:01:34.450
Your turn. Say: Music.

33
00:01:37.150 --> 00:01:38.140
Music.

34
00:01:39.150 --> 00:01:40.023
Budget.

35
00:01:40.723 --> 00:01:42.909
Budget means the amount of money you can spend.

36
00:01:43.209 --> 00:01:44.883
Our budget is fifty dollars.

37
00:01:45.583 --> 00:01:48.317
Your turn. Say: Budget.

38
00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:51.820
Budget.

39
00:01:52.817 --> 00:01:53.597
Plan.

40
00:01:54.297 --> 00:01:56.610
Plan means to decide what to do and how.

41
00:01:56.910 --> 00:01:58.306
We need to plan the party.

42
00:01:59.006 --> 00:02:01.554
Your turn. Say: Plan.

43
00:02:04.254 --> 00:02:04.976
Plan.

44
00:02:05.983 --> 00:02:07.902
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:08.202 --> 00:02:10.758
Class, let's plan a party for Teachers' Day!

46
00:02:12.050 --> 00:02:14.679
Great! We're going to decorate the classroom.

47
00:02:15.983 --> 00:02:17.518
Who will invite the guests?

48
00:02:18.817 --> 00:02:21.875
I'll do it! I'll write the invitations tonight.

49
00:02:23.183 --> 00:02:24.486
What about our budget?

50
00:02:25.783 --> 00:02:28.596
We're going to spend thirty dollars on food and drinks.

51
00:02:29.883 --> 00:02:32.278
Grammar focus: Will and going to.

52
00:02:32.578 --> 00:02:35.671
We will invite guests. We're going to decorate.

53
00:02:35.971 --> 00:02:40.595
Use 'going to' for plans you already made, and 'will' for decisions you make while speaking.

54
00:02:41.583 --> 00:02:44.607
Now read and listen. A Party for Our Teacher.

55
00:02:44.907 --> 00:02:46.918
We are planning a party for our teacher.

56
00:02:48.217 --> 00:02:50.959
First, we will invite guests and write invitations.

57
00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:55.341
Then, we're going to decorate the classroom with balloons.

58
00:02:56.650 --> 00:02:59.683
We will plan food and music and stay within our budget.

59
00:03:00.983 --> 00:03:03.227
It's going to be a wonderful surprise!

60
00:03:04.517 --> 00:03:06.995
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:07.295 --> 00:03:09.167
We're blank to decorate the room.

62
00:03:09.467 --> 00:03:12.911
A, going. B, go. C, will.

63
00:03:16.917 --> 00:03:18.684
The answer is A: going.

64
00:03:20.183 --> 00:03:22.427
A person who is invited is a blank.

65
00:03:22.727 --> 00:03:25.962
A, guest. B, budget. C, plan.

66
00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:32.124
The answer is A: guest.

67
00:03:33.617 --> 00:03:35.500
The money you can spend is your blank.

68
00:03:35.800 --> 00:03:38.734
A, budget. B, party. C, music.

69
00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:44.424
The answer is A: budget.

70
00:03:45.917 --> 00:03:49.010
Now it's your turn to speak. What do you need to plan a party?

71
00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:59.911
We need a budget, a guest list, food and music. We're going to decorate, and I'll make the cake.

72
00:04:00.211 --> 00:04:01.967
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:02.983 --> 00:04:07.203
Great work today! You learned eight new words and will and going to.

74
00:04:07.503 --> 00:04:11.386
Today's value is teamwork. We can do more when we work together.

75
00:04:11.686 --> 00:04:14.350
See you in Unit twenty-four. Goodbye!

76
00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.546
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

